content:
The picture is now clear. Before t=489, orders reach "fulfilled" normally (956 rows) with almost none stuck at "invoiced" (1 row). After t=489, orders are getting stuck at "invoiced" (58 rows) and a new "paid" status appears (25 rows, starting at t=598). No "confirmed" status exists at all — the invariant requires "confirmed" but the system never produces it post-deploy. The deploy at t=489 refactored webhook error handling and silently swallowed the confirmation callback, leaving orders in "invoiced"/"paid" instead of advancing to "confirmed". No webhook errors are logged (E10) because the refactored error handling is suppressing them.

